:0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I added `removeItem(cart, sku)` to `src/cart.js`. It builds a new cart with a filtered copy of `items`, so the original cart is never changed. If the SKU isn't in the cart, you get back a new cart that is deep-equal to the original.\n\n```js\nexport const removeItem = (cart, sku) => ({ ...cart, items: cart.items.filter(i => i.sku !== sku) })\n```\n\nI also added three tests to `test/cart.test.js`: removing a SKU drops only that item, an unknown SKU returns an equal cart, and the original cart doesn't change. The full suite passes (11 of 11).\n\nI also noticed what looks like a bug in `calcTotal` (`src/cart.js:24`), and I didn't change it. `taxable` is `applyCoupon(subtotal - discount, cart.coupon)`, so the coupon is applied twice: once in `discount` and again here. That means carts with a coupon get taxed and totaled on an amount that's too low. The existing total test uses no coupon, so it doesn't catch this. The fix is probably `const taxable = subtotal - discount`. Want me to make that change and add a test with a coupon?","ttft_ms":2329,"type":"result","duration_ms":20843,"uuid":"61738a34-6bf8-4946-89f0-4fb813d7d3c4","ttft_stream_ms":1782,"time_to_request_ms":181,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":39,"system_prompt":63,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":21,"engine_pickup":16,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"query_setup":2,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":56,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":266,"time_to_request_major_faults":6370,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"queued_commands","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":16,"major_faults":386},"first_content_frame_ms":1783,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
